'
'CR3000 Datalogger
'TA54B 10-Meter Tower Site Program
' 
'
' Notice: Requires Compilation in PipeLineMode for CSAT3B Ultrsonic Anemometer
'################################################################################
'########## Program Comments & Notes###########Program Comments & Notes####
'################################################################################
'###############################################################################
'
' Revision History:
' Revision History:
'
'
'
'
'
'
'Date:June 9th, 2021 GTStanton
'Updated program data labels as follows
  'For 15-Min Data Table
      'HWDir1_StdDev  to sddir1
  'HWSpd1-ms-StdDev to sdspd1
  '
  'For 24-Hr Data Table
  'HWSpd1-ms-Avg  to  avgspd1
  'For above need to change root tag/label from "HWSpd1" to "avgspd1"
'
'
' _6gts_11-10-2020 went through program and removed excess items carried over from
'example programs of MetTestStation & TA5MDCN to minimize confusion & Transferred in
' notes from Robert Carpenters work on initial purchase request Feb 25, 2020 for program.
'
'
'
' Sensors Installed:
' 1-RM Young 05305AQ Horizontal Anemometers
' 1-RM Young 27106T Gill Anemometer [Vertical Wind Speed Config.]
' 2-RMYoung 43347-41432 Temp Sensor w/Aspiration Fans
' 1-CSI Model CSAT3B Ultrasonic Anemometer.
' 1-RM Young Model 81000 Ultrasonic 3D Anemometer.
' 1-CSI Leaf Sensor
'
'NOTES FROM ROBERT CARPENTER MODIFICATIONS FOR INITIAL PROGRAM FEB 25, 2020
'Changes to this version:
'  1.Added the instruction to measure a CSAT3B sensor.  All coding (i.e.
'    Variable names, measurement instructions, data types) were ported over
'    from a program named MetTestStationRev_4_10012019.CR3. Both the sample
'    program, MetTestStationRev_4_10012019 and the proram that was to be
'    added to, TA5 MDCN_V4.CR3 were provided by Gregory T Stanton.
'    ##### Though every effort to make sure this new program functions as
'          it has been requested, the data from this new program should be
'          closely reviewed for accuracy before proceeding with any long
'          term testing.#####
'  2. See wiring instructions for the CSAT3B below.
'  3. Changed from SequentialMode to PipeLineMode
'  4. Added instructions to measure the RPM of the fan on the 43502
'     aspirated radiation shield and added the output to the 15 minute
'     data table.
'  5. Replaced the 060A2 air temp sensors with the RM Young 43347 air temp
'     sensor and added the output to the 15 minute data table.
'  6. Added the CSI Leaf Wetness sensor and added the output to the 15
'     minute data table.
'  7. Added more output instructions to the 15 minute data table for the
'     Battery Voltage measurement.
'  8. Added more output instructions to the 15 minute data table for the
'     RM Young 05305AQ anemometer.
'  9. Added more output instructions to the 15 minute data table for the
'     RM Young 27106T Vertical anemometer.
'  10. Deleted/Removed all instructions pertaining to the Eppley 8-48
'      sensor.
'  11. Corrected the wiring description listed below, and before the program
'      starts, to match the measureemnt instruction in the program. Some of
'      the channel assigments did not match.  This new version should be
'      used for wiring up the new sensors.
'  12. Added the instruction to include the RM Young 81000 3D sonic with
'      Serial Output. The sensor is connected to 12V, G and Com4 (C7&C8).
'      Program example from Knowledge Base
'SET PARAMETERS (RMY81000 firmware 7.0.05)
'A) AVERAGING = 0
'B) BAUD = 38400
'E) ERROR HANDLING = INCLUDE INVALID DATA
'N) SCALING MULT = NA
'O) OUTPUT RATE = 32 Hz
'P) POLL CHARACTER (ADDR) = NA
'S) SER OUT FORMAT = CUSTOM - UVW, Ts, ERR CODE, CHKSUM
'T) THRESHOD = 20
'U) UNITS = m/s
'V) V OUT FORMAT = NA
'W) WAKE CORRECTION = YES
'
'program change on 11/13/2020
'81000 readings appear to be swapped, cannot lower tower to verify wiring so this revision will swap:
'SE11 and SE12 for the VoltSE measurements with respect to Wind Speed and Wind Direction
'SE13 and SE14 for the VoltSE measurements with respect to the Elevation and Temperature
'also uncommented the Ux, Uy and Uz section of the 15 minute table so those values can be recorded
'###############################################################################
'###############################################################################
'##### -Wiring Configuration for CR3000- #######################################
'###############################################################################
'###############################################################################
'
' RMYoung 05305-AQ Wind Speed & Direction Sensor (1)
'    1H:  HWDir Signal Yellow
'    Ground:  WSpd reference Green
'    Ground:  Cable Shield White
'    Ground:  WDir reference Black
'    VX1:  HWDir Excite Blue
'    P1:  HWspd Signal Red
'
'  RMYoung 27106T Wind Speed Sensor (1)
'    3H:  VWspd Signal Red
'    Ground:  WSpd reference Black
'    Ground:  Cable Shield Clear?
'
'  RM Young 43347 Air Temp Sensor L-1
'    4H: Air Temp Signal High White
'    4L: Air Temp Signal Low Green
'    IX1: Switched Current Excitation Red
'    IXR: Excitation Return Black
'    AG: Shield Clear
'    P2: Tachometer White
'    G:  Ground for fan Tach Red
'    G: Shield Black
'
'  RM Young 43347 Air Temp Sensor L-2
'    5H: Air Temp Signal High White
'    5L: Air Temp Signal Low Green
'    IX2: Switched Current Excitation Red
'    IXR: Excitation Return Black
'    AG: Shield Clear
'    P3: Tachometer White
'    G:  Ground for fan Tach Red
'    G: Shield Black
'
'  CSI Leaf Wetness Sensor
'    2H: Sensor Out  Orange or Red
'    VX3: Sensor Excitation Brown or White
'    AG: Analog Ground Clear
'
' CSAT3B
'  CSAT3B Sonic Anemometer
'    SDM INPUT (CSAT3B SDM address = 3)
'    SDM-C1   CSAT3B SDM Data (green)
'    SDM-C2   CSAT3B SDM Clock (white)
'    SDM-C3   CSAT3B SDM Enable (brown)
'    G    CSAT3B SDM reference (black)
'    G    CSAT3B SDM shield (clear)
'    POWER IN
'    12V  datalogger (red)
'    G  datalogger (black)
'    EXTERNAL POWER SUPPLY
'    POS  CSAT3B power (red)
'      datalogger (red)
'    NEG  CSAT3B power reference (black)
'
' RM Young 81000 (wired for Voltage Signal Output)
'  12V-2:      Power to Sensor (Red)
'  G:          Sensor Power Ground (White & Black)
'  6H: (SE11)  V1 Wind Speed  (Green)
'  6L: (SE12)  V2 Wind Direction (Blue)
'  7H: (SE13)  V3 Elevation (Yellow)
'  7L: (SE14)  V4 Temperature (Orange)
'  AG          VRef (Brown)
'
'
'
'
'
'
'
'
'
'
'################################################################################
'################################################################################
'##### Define & Declare Constants, Variables & Aliases  ########################
'################################################################################
'################################################################################
'Note: In Order for the CSAT3B Sonic Anemometer to function properly
'the program must be set up to run in "PipeLineMode" instead of our LANL existing
'"SequentialMode". This limit may require us to slow down the program
'sequence/run time to greater than the 3-second standard.

'Const PScan=3  'enter program execution interval in seconds
'
PipeLineMode
AngleDegrees     'program is expecting trig numbers in degress (as opposed to Radians)

'
Const Scan_Rate = 1
'Definitions & Declarations for General Sensors.
Public BattV, PTemp_C
Public avgspd1_ms, HWDir1_deg
Public VWSpd1_ms,
Public AirTemp1_43347_DegC
Public AirTemp2_43347_DegC

Public RTD_Res_1, RTD_Res_2
Const T1_Co1 = -251.132627
Const T1_Co2 = 2.398537E-1
Const T1_Co3 = 1.127887E-5
Const T2_Co1 = -251.132627
Const T2_Co2 = 2.398637E-1
Const T2_Co3 = 1.127887E-5
Public Tach_Hz_1, Tach_Hz_2
Public LWmV
Public LWMDry
Public LWMCon
Public LWMWet


Public mxgst1, dirgst1,HW1Max24HrTime(9)
Public HWSpd2Max24Hr, HWDir2Max24Hr,HW2Max24HrTime(9)
Public HWSpd3Max24Hr, HWDir3Max24Hr,HW3Max24HrTime(9)
Public HWSpd4Max24Hr, HWDir4Max24Hr,HW4Max24HrTime(9)
'
Public avgspd1_1min, HWDir1_1min, HWTime1_1min(9)
Public mx1gst, dir1gst, HWTime1_max1min(9)

'
'===========================================================================
'Variables added 1/26/17 by Jason Ritter for 15 minute update to Public table
Public PrecipToday, MaxGustToday,WindChill_15min
Dim WindChill_C,WindChill_F, temp0_F, speed1_mph 'Variables for wind chill calculation
Public SigmaPhi, SigmaTheta
Public V_PGCat As String
Public H_PGCat As String
Public Sun As Boolean

'RMY81000
Public WSpd81000
Public WDir81000
Public EleveAngle81000 'Preserve this unnecessary variable to maintain ordering.
Public TempC81000
Public VertWS81000
